<title>SWITZERLAND: Schindler in 58.7 mln Sfr tram deal.</title>
<headline>Schindler in 58.7 mln Sfr tram deal.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortium led by Swiss engineering concern Schindler Holding AG has received an order worth 58.7 million Swiss francs to build trams for the city of Zurich, Schindler said in a press release.</p>
<p>&quot;With a budget of 58.7 million francs, the transport authorities of the city of Zurich are laying ground for a new generation of trams,&quot; Schindler said.</p>
<p>The deal, under direction of Schindler Waggon, includes FIAT-SIG Schienenfahrzeuge AG and ABB Daimler-Benz Transportation AG (Adtranz).</p>
<p>It calls for initial delivery of six trams in 1999, and a further 11 in 2002. -- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
